<article class="env-remark" id="047O">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/047O">Remark <span data-tag="047O">39.8.3</span>.</a> Any group scheme over a field of characteristic $0$ is reduced, see <span class="cite">[<span class="postnote">I, Theorem 1.1 and I, Corollary 3.9, and II, Theorem 2.4</span>, <a href="/bibliography/Perrin-thesis">Perrin-thesis</a>]</span> and also <span class="cite">[<span class="postnote">Proposition 4.2.8</span>, <a href="/bibliography/Perrin">Perrin</a>]</span>. This was a question raised in <span class="cite">[<span class="postnote">page 80</span>, <a href="/bibliography/Oort">Oort</a>]</span>. We have seen in Lemma <a href="/tag/047N" data-tag="047N">39.8.2</a> that this holds when the group scheme is locally of finite type. </p>
</article>